WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.560 --> 00:00:06.880
Hi, Mystery Recapped here. Today I am going&nbsp;
to explain the German satirical comedy film&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:06.880 --> 00:00:16.080
called “Look Who’s Back.” Spoilers&nbsp;
ahead! Watch out and take care!
&nbsp;

00:00:16.080 --> 00:00:22.320
The beginning of the movie is set somewhere during&nbsp;
the second world war in Berlin. The Fuhrer Hitler&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:22.320 --> 00:00:27.520
is with a behaviour coach named Keppl. Hitler&nbsp;
expresses his disagreement with the gesture of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:27.520 --> 00:00:32.800
people's greeting to Keppl. He complains that&nbsp;
though the Nazi salute is out-fashioned, people&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:32.800 --> 00:00:38.480
need to at least raise their hands up to the wrist&nbsp;
and show respect. Then, he narrates that he has&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:38.480 --> 00:00:43.600
done everything possible by a human to destroy&nbsp;
the foundations of the enemy who desecrated their&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:43.600 --> 00:00:49.360
soil. He finds German's existence incomprehensible&nbsp;
and finds it alarming that he is here too.
&nbsp;

00:00:50.000 --> 00:00:55.040
In the following scene, he wakes up on the ground&nbsp;
somewhere in a forest. While looking up to the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:55.040 --> 00:01:00.560
sky, he sees that the enemy aircrafts are missing&nbsp;
and guesses that they might have taken some rest.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:00.560 --> 00:01:06.480
Suddenly, a ball comes bouncing towards him and&nbsp;
stops just at his side. He raises himself and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:06.480 --> 00:01:12.080
heads towards a building past the bush. He is then&nbsp;
approached by three young kids who question him&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:12.080 --> 00:01:16.000
if he is okay. Hitler looks at them and&nbsp;
thinks that they are the future of the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:16.000 --> 00:01:22.080
nation. He then asks them the way to the street.&nbsp;
In that instant, a reporter, Fabian Sawatzki,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:22.080 --> 00:01:27.200
is filming the kids on his camera. Hitler is&nbsp;
seen on the far side of the screen. He picks&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:27.200 --> 00:01:32.400
up his army cap and says to himself that he should&nbsp;
go to the Fuhrer Bunker. Hitler gets to the street&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:32.400 --> 00:01:37.920
and gets amazed at people riding monowheel bikes.&nbsp;
He finds people capturing him in their camera and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:37.920 --> 00:01:44.080
expresses that though the rubble went, people have&nbsp;
gone mad. Then, he feels a modern car by his hand&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:44.080 --> 00:01:49.440
and questions himself if he fell in a coma and&nbsp;
missed the victory. He realises that he is not&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:49.440 --> 00:01:55.440
aware of his situation totally and alerts himself&nbsp;
to collect more information. Then, he asks a man&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:55.440 --> 00:02:00.800
about the location of Chancellery but the person&nbsp;
instead asks him for a picture. He gets disturbed&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:00.800 --> 00:02:07.120
by the camera's flashes as people come near him&nbsp;
and take photos in turns. Confused by the unusual&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:07.120 --> 00:02:12.640
events around him, he concludes something went&nbsp;
out of hand in the place. As Hitler walks away,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:12.640 --> 00:02:17.760
he finds a woman speaking in German on her phone.&nbsp;
He comes closer and asks her about the current&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:17.760 --> 00:02:23.680
date, but the woman gets terrified and sprays his&nbsp;
eyes. Hitler cries in pain as his eyes get reddish&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:23.680 --> 00:02:29.200
and his vision gets blurred. He stumbles and&nbsp;
walks to a newspaper shop nearby. He gets&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:29.200 --> 00:02:36.160
shocked to see the date October 3, 2014, written&nbsp;
on the paper and falls to the ground at once.
&nbsp;

00:02:36.160 --> 00:02:42.080
Somewhere else, the boss of a TV station,&nbsp;
Karrner, praises Mr. Christoph Sensenbrink for his&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:42.080 --> 00:02:47.920
excellent job as the deputy's head. He proposes&nbsp;
a higher solution but instead announces another&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:47.920 --> 00:02:54.400
worker named Miss Katja Bellini as the managing&nbsp;
director. Due to this, Christoph gets shocked and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:54.400 --> 00:03:00.720
dissatisfied. He comes to his office and vents his&nbsp;
anger out at a struggling filmmaker named Fabian.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:00.720 --> 00:03:06.160
Despite Fabian’s best attempts to convince his&nbsp;
boss, he gets fired and thrown out by the guards.
&nbsp;

00:03:06.720 --> 00:03:12.160
Some time later, Hitler wakes up at the news shop&nbsp;
and asks the owner about the date. He confirms&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:12.160 --> 00:03:17.840
that it is in fact 2014. A confused Hitler&nbsp;
questions if the shopkeeper has kidnapped him&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:17.840 --> 00:03:23.280
and suspects if all this is a trick play of the&nbsp;
enemy's secret service. He threatens to kill the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:23.280 --> 00:03:28.960
shopkeeper if he is working for the enemy but the&nbsp;
shopkeeper gives him a bar of chocolate instead.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:28.960 --> 00:03:35.040
Hitler opens it after quite a struggle and sniffs&nbsp;
it. He declares it as industrially pressed grain&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:35.040 --> 00:03:40.080
and questions the shopkeeper if there is still a&nbsp;
shortage of bread. The shopkeeper asks Hitler if&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:40.080 --> 00:03:45.200
they are filming a documentary somewhere nearby,&nbsp;
mistaking him for an actor. The shopkeeper then&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:45.200 --> 00:03:50.960
says that he looks exactly like the Fuhrer to&nbsp;
which Hitler replies that he is the Fuhrer.
&nbsp;

00:03:50.960 --> 00:03:57.600
After that, Hitler sees the Turkish newspaper and&nbsp;
asks if the shopkeeper has Sturmer or Panzerbar.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:57.600 --> 00:04:02.240
The shopkeeper says that he has more Turkish&nbsp;
customers. Hitler gets astonished at the presence&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:02.240 --> 00:04:06.960
of Turkish people in Berlin. He then starts&nbsp;
collecting information from the newspaper.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:06.960 --> 00:04:11.760
While reading it, he assumes that he didn’t win&nbsp;
the war in the past and Germany was given to the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:11.760 --> 00:04:17.680
hands of clumsy women having the charisma of a wet&nbsp;
noodle. He further laments the existence of Poland&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:17.680 --> 00:04:23.280
and concludes the war to be a total waste.
Meanwhile, Fabian looks upon his video reporting&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:23.280 --> 00:04:33.040
about soccer and sobs, sad at the fact that he&nbsp;
was fired. His mother calms him and asks him to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:33.040 --> 00:04:38.640
pause the video, noticing Hitler behind. Fabian&nbsp;
is amused at the discovery of a person who looks&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:38.640 --> 00:04:44.320
so similar to Hitler. Back in the shop, the&nbsp;
shopkeeper asks Hitler to keep the newspaper aside&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:44.320 --> 00:04:50.480
and stand outside. Hitler grudges at being asked&nbsp;
to work. The shopkeeper suggests Hitler clean his&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:50.480 --> 00:04:55.200
clothes, for they are stinking. He then goes&nbsp;
to a laundry place and asks them to clean his&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:55.200 --> 00:04:59.760
uniform. Hitler asks if they have another&nbsp;
uniform since he cannot walk away naked. 
&nbsp;

00:05:05.200 --> 00:05:11.680
Next, we see Hitler walking to the news&nbsp;
seller with jeans and a sweater on. Fabian,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:11.680 --> 00:05:16.960
on the other hand, has somehow managed to find him&nbsp;
and is waiting for him in the shop. After getting&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:16.960 --> 00:05:22.720
a look at Hitler, he is amazed at his appearance.&nbsp;
Fabian asks Hitler if he can film him as he&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:22.720 --> 00:05:28.480
marches through modern Germany. Hitler agrees with&nbsp;
the idea. Fabian takes up some cash and a car from&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:28.480 --> 00:05:33.680
his mother and starts his journey with Hitler.
The two end up in a hotel where Hitler gets&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:33.680 --> 00:05:39.200
amused at seeing the television. He then decides&nbsp;
to talk about Politics in Fabian's presentation.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:39.200 --> 00:05:44.800
He goes to places asking people regarding their&nbsp;
views on politics. After the interviews, he finds&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:44.800 --> 00:05:50.720
that there was minimal impact of democracy upon&nbsp;
people during his absence. He inspects discontent&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:50.720 --> 00:05:56.640
and suppressed anger in people which reminds him&nbsp;
of the 1930s, when people had similar views but&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:56.640 --> 00:06:01.200
lacked the term 'Political disenchantment'.&nbsp;
People tell Hitler about the problem of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:01.200 --> 00:06:05.840
immigrants in the country making Hitler push&nbsp;
his idea that mixing the races doesn't work.
&nbsp;

00:06:06.400 --> 00:06:11.840
Later, Fabian asks Hitler the source of his&nbsp;
unique mustache. Hitler replies that he cut his&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:11.840 --> 00:06:17.600
mustache to the shape to fit a gas mask. A while&nbsp;
later, the two end up in a farm where Hitler gets&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:17.600 --> 00:06:23.760
bit by a dog. He is enraged and shoots at the&nbsp;
animal. Fabian scolds him and seizes the gun.
&nbsp;

00:06:23.760 --> 00:06:29.520
As the tour goes on, Fabian eventually runs out&nbsp;
of cash. But he thinks of a plan and convinces&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:29.520 --> 00:06:37.040
the passers to have their sketches drawn by&nbsp;
Hitler. Hitler draws sarcastic pictures which&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:37.040 --> 00:06:42.000
people find funny and pay for it. They continue&nbsp;
their trip after collecting enough money.
&nbsp;

00:06:42.560 --> 00:06:48.400
Back in town, Fabian shows a clip of Hitler to&nbsp;
Christoph. The video has a lot of views as Fabian&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:48.400 --> 00:06:52.480
had uploaded it on the internet. Christoph&nbsp;
is impressed by the large number of views&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:52.480 --> 00:06:57.840
in the video. He asks Fabian for Hitler’s&nbsp;
name and contact number. After meeting him,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:57.840 --> 00:07:03.120
Christoph suspects Hitler to be a lunatic and&nbsp;
asks Fabian to take him away from the office.
&nbsp;

00:07:03.120 --> 00:07:08.240
Before leaving, Hitler enters the director’s&nbsp;
office and asks her to save Germany together&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:08.240 --> 00:07:12.640
with him. Interested at the idea,&nbsp;
Bellini asks him about the plan.
&nbsp;

00:07:12.640 --> 00:07:18.080
She quickly asks her assistant to prepare a proper&nbsp;
TV format for broadcasting the Fuhrer on listening&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:18.080 --> 00:07:23.440
to Hitler's idea. Fabian then threatens Christoph&nbsp;
to give him his job back or else he will take&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:23.440 --> 00:07:29.040
Hitler away. On hearing this, Christoph makes him&nbsp;
a kitchen boy promising to promote him when a new&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:29.040 --> 00:07:37.840
editorial post opens up. Some time later, Hitler&nbsp;
is given a table in the TV studio. Christoph&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:37.840 --> 00:07:43.440
calls for Kromeier to help Hitler with computer&nbsp;
use. Hitler recalls the computers of his days and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:43.440 --> 00:07:48.560
labels the invention to be one of the greatest.&nbsp;
Kromeier tries to sign up Hitler to mail but&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:48.560 --> 00:07:53.840
informs him that his name is already taken. Hitler&nbsp;
grunts for others stealing his name and tells her&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:53.840 --> 00:07:59.920
to use 'New Reichs Chancellery' as he liked it. 
Christoph plans to put Hitler on a live comedy&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:59.920 --> 00:08:05.600
show called Whoa Dude! He is still salty&nbsp;
because Bellini got a promotion instead of him&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:05.600 --> 00:08:10.400
and intends to create trouble for her. He&nbsp;
intends to bring racism to the debate through&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:10.400 --> 00:08:17.040
sarcastic jokes on Jews and throw out Hitler.
The show starts, and Witzigman, the host, calls&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:17.040 --> 00:08:22.240
for Hitler on the stage. The audience gossips&nbsp;
about Hitler's appearance but when Hitler gazes&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:22.240 --> 00:08:27.760
at the audience, the hall gets completely silent.&nbsp;
Hitler soon breaks the silence but does not read&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:27.760 --> 00:08:33.280
out the lines as scripted. He explains that he&nbsp;
is to tell a joke about immigrants but he is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:33.280 --> 00:08:38.960
not going to do so. He says that a TV is a great&nbsp;
invention of the human, but the shows broadcasted&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:38.960 --> 00:08:47.120
are nonsense. He sheds light on problems like&nbsp;
poverty and unemployment and forecasts that the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:47.120 --> 00:08:52.080
people of the country are heading towards the&nbsp;
abyss without noticing it. Hitler vows to fight&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:52.080 --> 00:08:57.360
against the TV not only up to the broadcast&nbsp;
of the abyss but also until he succeeds in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:57.360 --> 00:09:02.960
overcoming them. Everyone likes the idea and&nbsp;
claps for him. Seeing Hitler's popularity,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:02.960 --> 00:09:09.520
the host Witzigman gets envious. Bellini asks&nbsp;
Christoph to broadcast Hitler in every show.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:09.520 --> 00:09:14.880
Christoph is distressed because of the failure of&nbsp;
his plan. In the following scene, we see Hitler&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:14.880 --> 00:09:22.640
give interviews on numerous TV shows and share&nbsp;
that his motive is to make Germany great again.
&nbsp;

00:09:24.320 --> 00:09:29.360
His popularity grows immensely and he meets&nbsp;
several people and party leaders. He starts&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:29.360 --> 00:09:35.520
charming them all by sharing his ideas. One&nbsp;
day, Hitler and Fabian visit NPD headquarters&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:35.520 --> 00:09:41.280
in Berlin. He calls for Ulf Birne, the Federal&nbsp;
Chairman of NPD and asks him what his cause&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:41.280 --> 00:09:45.920
has achieved so far. Hitler belittles him&nbsp;
and says that they have wasted enough time,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:45.920 --> 00:09:50.080
and the movement is taken aback&nbsp;
by decades due to their words.
&nbsp;

00:09:50.080 --> 00:09:55.920
Christoph gets excited and happy when the cops&nbsp;
and District Attorney (DA) appear at the TV&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:55.920 --> 00:10:01.120
studio. They explain that they are here for a&nbsp;
complaint of charging violation of hate laws.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:01.120 --> 00:10:06.080
Bellini asks what they are to do then. Quickly,&nbsp;
Christoph pops that they might need to cancel the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:06.080 --> 00:10:11.600
Fuhrer show. The DA says that they can keep the&nbsp;
broadcasting on. Bellini takes a sigh of relief&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:11.600 --> 00:10:16.240
while Christoph fakes his smile.
After the DA leaves, Kromeier hands&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:16.240 --> 00:10:20.880
over a letter to Christoph stating the payment&nbsp;
of the dog which Hitler had shot earlier in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:20.880 --> 00:10:25.760
his trip. Christoph receives the letter happily&nbsp;
believing it might be a way to cause trouble.
&nbsp;

00:10:25.760 --> 00:10:30.880
Next, Hitler is put to a TV program where he&nbsp;
is asked direct questions about his different&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:30.880 --> 00:10:35.760
roles in the war. Hitler responds that he wants to&nbsp;
reach out to people but the interviewer tells him&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:35.760 --> 00:10:41.520
